CCTPBridgeModuleFork
├── constructor
│   ├── it should set tokenMessenger to real TokenMessengerV2 address
│   ├── it should set usdc to real USDC address
│   └── it should return CCTP_BRIDGE as moduleType
├── ABI compatibility
│   ├── it should confirm TokenMessengerV2 is deployed at fork block
│   ├── it should call depositForBurn on real TokenMessengerV2 successfully
│   └── it should call depositForBurnWithHook on real TokenMessengerV2 successfully
├── execute
│   ├── it should decrease paymentRails USDC balance by bridge amount
│   ├── it should leave module with zero USDC after burn
│   ├── it should revoke module approval to TokenMessengerV2 after burn
│   ├── it should emit BridgeInitiated event
│   ├── it should return success result with correct amountOut
│   ├── given params with hook data
│   │   ├── it should burn USDC successfully
│   │   └── it should emit BridgeInitiated with hookData
│   ├── it should succeed on consecutive bridges
│   ├── it should succeed with small amount (100 USDC)
│   └── it should succeed with fast finality threshold
├── validate
│   ├── it should return true for valid params
│   ├── it should return false for non-USDC token
│   ├── it should return false for zero amount
│   ├── it should return false for zero mint recipient
│   ├── it should return false for invalid finality threshold
│   ├── it should return false when maxFee exceeds amount
│   ├── it should return false for insufficient balance
│   └── it should return false for invalid params encoding
├── estimateOutput
│   ├── it should return full amount when maxFee is zero
│   ├── it should return amount minus maxFee
│   └── it should return zero for invalid params
├── paymentRails integration lifecycle
│   ├── it should bridge successfully via PaymentRails.executeAction end-to-end
│   ├── it should emit ActionExecuted from PaymentRails
│   ├── it should return correct previewExecution values
│   ├── it should succeed on consecutive executions draining the paymentRails
│   └── it should bridge from two paymentRails sharing one module
└── security
    ├── it should always have zero approval to TokenMessengerV2 after execute
    ├── it should hold no USDC after multiple bridges
    ├── it should allow any address to execute (permissionless)
    ├── it should confirm real USDC has 6 decimals
    ├── it should confirm real USDC burn reduces total supply
    └── it should consume paymentRails-to-module approval after execute
